# This mod ships no assembly and has nothing to build, so the compilation rules below are
# inherited convention rather than a live need. The entry that earns its place here is
# .claude/: a session worktree is a full copy of the repository it is made in, hundreds of
# megabytes when that was the monorepo, and one has already landed inside a mod folder once.
#
# Two separate reasons to have this file, and only the first is about git:
#
#   - This folder is its own repository, so nothing above it covers any of this. It sat in a
#     monorepo until 2026-09-11, and even then the root rules did not travel with the exported
#     folder, so the file has always had to stand on its own.
#   - Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's
#     target directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the
#     published folder is published. That is what `Mod/` is for: the junction points there,
#     and everything else in this folder - Art/, the docs, this file - stays out of reach by
#     construction.

# Build intermediates.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# DDS byproducts: RimWorld (or its Workshop uploader) drops a compressed .dds beside every
# .png it imports, inside the same folder — found on 2026-09-28, 222 of them dated
# 2026-09-23, all in Mod/Textures next to the shipped PNGs. Steam publishes whatever sits on
# disk in Mod/ with no filtering, so an uncleaned .dds is dead weight in the Workshop item,
# not a second copy of anything the game reads. Never commit one; delete on sight before a publish.
*.dds

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings: each worktree is a full copy of a repository,
# and they are never shared.
.claude/

# Showcase notes: French working notes, deleted once Preview.png and ModIcon.png are done.
PROMPT_*.md

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Explorer artifact leak into the published folder: found live here on 2026-09-28, a
# Mod/desktop.ini pointing at ..\Art\Preview.ico (root desktop.ini and Art/*.ico stay fine,
# they sit outside Mod/, which Steam sends as-is). git never tracked it - desktop.ini above
# already covers that - but it still sat on disk where a publish would have picked it up.
# Same precedent at A Certain Series, 2026-09-27. Belt and suspenders: block it by path too.
Mod/desktop.ini
Mod/**/*.ico

# Pickle evidence stays on disk, never in git (AGENTS.md): captures and Player.log grow without limit.
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
evidence/

# Reproducible Preview diagnostics generated locally by the shared renderer.
Art/.render/
